  "While formatters have their place in certain contexts, I want you to focus on developing a strong understanding of code structure and formatting by hand.",
  "It's important to grasp the fundamentals first.",
  "When you rely on formatters too heavily, you might lose the opportunity to truly internalize the syntax and structure of the language.",
  "When you write code without a formatter, you're forced to pay attention to the intricacies of indentation, whitespace, and syntax.",
  "These details are crucial for writing clean, readable, and maintainable code.",
  "Absolutely.",
  "It's a matter of developing good habits from the start.",
  "When you write code by hand, you train your brain to think like a programmer.",
  "You'll become more mindful of code style, readability, and best practices."
 ],
